# SERVER-TO-SERVER example; placeholders only, not real credentials.
# The browser uses its human identity, never the consumer's long-lived M2M key.
@baseUrl = https://helpdesk.example.invalid
@session = REPLACE_WITH_SHORT_SESSION
@workspace = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### Discover accounts, product instances and services authorized for the current principal.
# Requires contexts:resolve. Returns zero, one or several options; no automatic contract choice.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/support-contexts?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{session}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspace}}

### Next page: URL-encode the exact next_cursor, with the same identity/workspace/filter.
# Do not reuse cursor across identities. Discovery is live, not a snapshot/reservation.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/support-contexts?limit=50&cursor=REPLACE_WITH_URL_ENCODED_CURSOR
Authorization: Bearer {{session}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspace}}

### Resolve a chosen option; below are synthetic example identifiers, not existing resources.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/contexts/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{session}}
X-Workspace-Id: {{workspace}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101",
  "product_instance_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000401",
  "service_code": "SUPPORT"
}

# On ambiguous: show candidates and require explicit coverage_id at creation.
# On no_coverage: do not invent a contract. Intakes are not implemented yet.
# POST /v1/tickets revalidates scope/coverage again and requires Idempotency-Key.
# Selecting or retaining an option does not override a later suspension/revocation.
